-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Expat and miniz (linked, not bundled)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Neither library's source is in this package, but both are compiled into it.
zuxlsx links libzuxml.a and libzukomp.a statically at install time, so an
installed or binary zuxlsx contains Expat and miniz object code and therefore
redistributes both. Their licences require the notices below to travel with
that code, which is why they appear here rather than only in the packages the
archives come from.

Both are MIT.

  Expat (libexpat), from zuxml
      Copyright (c) 1998-2000 Thai Open Source Software Center Ltd and
                              Clark Cooper
      Copyright (c) 2001-2025 Expat maintainers

      Full text: inst/licenses/expat-LICENSE
      Upstream:  https://github.com/libexpat/libexpat
      The source, its pinned release and its checksum are in zuxml; this
      package carries no copy of it.

  miniz, from zukomp
      Copyright 2013-2014 RAD Game Tools and Valve Software
      Copyright 2010-2014 Rich Geldreich and Tenacious Software LLC

      Full text: inst/licenses/miniz-LICENSE
      Upstream:  https://github.com/richgel999/miniz
      As above: the source and its provenance live in zukomp.

Only the reader side of each is linked in. Expat contributes its parser;
miniz contributes DEFLATE and the ZIP reader. Neither library's own tests,
utilities or build systems are involved.
